title: politicalDemand
---
<b>A Favour Remembered</b>
The petition bears the seal of {PoliticalCreditor()}. Their spokesman recalls the help once placed at your disposal. The City needed them then; now they ask the Emperor to honour his obligation.
Choose how to settle one favour. Refusal suspends this faction's passive benefit and special action for fifteen days; the debt remains.
-> Pay {PoliticalPayment()} gold from the treasury. <<if PoliticalCanPay()>>
    <<ResolvePoliticalDemand pay>>
    The sum is counted before witnesses. One obligation is discharged.
-> {PoliticalConcession()}
    <<ResolvePoliticalDemand concede>>
    The concession is proclaimed. One obligation is discharged, though others at court resent its price.
-> Give them greater authority at court. Faction influence +5 points. <<if PoliticalCanEmpower()>>
    <<ResolvePoliticalDemand empower>>
    <<if true>>
        Their place at council is strengthened. One obligation is discharged.
    <<endif>>
-> Refuse. Their passive benefit and special action are suspended for 15 days; the favour remains owed.
    <<ResolvePoliticalDemand refuse>>
    The delegation withdraws without satisfaction. For fifteen days their assistance is withheld. Their claim against the throne remains.
===
